{"title":"1976 IMO Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A box whose shape is a parallelepiped can be completely filled with cubes of side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/d/6cdd1b53e5faf7a118222e4b7571d1e9afa0cf56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> If we put in it the maximum possible number of cubes, each of volume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, with the sides parallel to those of the box, then exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> percent from the volume of the box is occupied. Determine the possible dimensions of the box.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We name a,b,c the sides of the parallelepiped, which are positive integers. We also put\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/e/01e5be93096638ffa23deef338bfcc258473e328.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} x &amp;= \\left\\lfloor\\frac{a}{\\sqrt[3]{2}}\\right\\rfloor \\\\ y &amp;= \\left\\lfloor\\frac{b}{\\sqrt[3]{2}}\\right\\rfloor \\\\ z &amp;= \\left\\lfloor\\frac{c}{\\sqrt[3]{2}}\\right\\rfloor \\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"79\" height=\"142\" />\nIt is clear that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/7/d57d8fef9329fabd73078ae824a034e8a00e332f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xyz$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"11\" /> is the maximal number of cubes with sides of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/d/9fdfe572d1673f00f286d5ed753942d18f401cbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt[3]{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"18\" /> that \ncan be put into the parallelepiped with sides parallels to the sides of the box.\nHence the corresponding volume is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/8/cc849ae7051632812cbb1006ff248b2858ca1889.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V_2=2\\cdot xyz$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" />. We need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/2/6c270c30c224cac1131cc547f61eddad6dbdd5f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V_2=0.4\\cdot V_1=0.4\\cdot abc$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"183\" height=\"15\" />,\nhence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/7/d6736042fadecb1e750d0451d7e643fdd490d7b6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac ax\\cdot \\frac by\\cdot \\frac cz=5\\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ (1)\\]\" width=\"164\" height=\"41\" />\nWe give the  values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/4/51412a110c75c35ecba3de4b23b49280db7e1662.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a/x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"18\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/2/4527a98ead89bc2f257bd6d98221869505101e6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=1,\\dots ,8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"92\" height=\"16\" />. The same table is valid for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/d/bfd77b57ea287e2c5a553f27c64c17b93f25e70f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b,y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/b/6bba5789d57444c113991cca955f3b1586754ad4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"24\" height=\"11\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/a/d0ad1b605175dbfe35f8aea432999b84df3c2bcf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{tabular}{|c|c|c|}   \\hline   a &amp; x &amp; a/x \\\\ \\hline   1 &amp; 0 &amp; - \\\\ \\hline   2 &amp; 1 &amp; 2 \\\\ \\hline   3 &amp; 2 &amp;  3/2 \\\\ \\hline   4 &amp; 3 &amp; 4/3 \\\\ \\hline   5 &amp; 3 &amp; 5/3 \\\\ \\hline   6 &amp; 4 &amp; 3/2 \\\\ \\hline   7 &amp; 5 &amp; 7/5 \\\\ \\hline   8 &amp; 6 &amp;  4/3 \\\\   \\hline \\end{tabular}\\]\" width=\"103\" height=\"186\" />\nBy simple inspection we obtain two solutions of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/a/7ea55431136ba8eacf03d1cced67bd2b3b9d54f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{a,b,c\\}=\\{2,5,3\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/d/0adfc5dcee40aab4b604f7ce22198f86ca5eaff9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{a,b,c\\}=\\{2,5,6\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" />.\nWe now show that they are the only solutions.\n</p><p>We can assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/2/6a20e80579b52f3fbc52b6504a099a73d33f6b49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac ax\\ge \\frac by \\ge \\frac cz$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"88\" height=\"41\" />. So necessarily <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/2/402522cc2c0e23ead7fb7ef5d401de21ee337232.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac ax\\ge \\sqrt[3]{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"64\" height=\"33\" />. Note that\nthe definition of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/3/c2322154ef2f498ecd2aaea6ed00f2e2c812ab4a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x&lt; a/\\sqrt[3]2 &lt; x+1,\\]\" width=\"147\" height=\"21\" />\nhence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/f/93f29517f67815d924cafa681ab885be0e2e53c5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt[3]2&lt; a/x &lt; \\sqrt[3]2(1+\\frac 1x)\\]\" width=\"184\" height=\"37\" />\nIf <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/c/fec3823b40bebb3b622559cc81335d75fe8635fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\ge 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"45\" height=\"16\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/0/7709fad7978c20741c4c917bb7b009bef6fb101c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\ge 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a05fa65a19f7ce168a043d889313cc88dec2d8d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac ax&lt;\\sqrt[3]2(1+\\frac 1x)\\le \\sqrt[3]2(\\frac 43)&lt;\\sqrt[3]5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"251\" height=\"38\" /> \nsince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/4/cc4a4e1145e1e5ceb9888d2de524eb5e972303d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot \\frac {4^3}{3^3}&lt;5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"75\" height=\"39\" />. So we have only left the cases <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/a/55afdab16c8c49089c4d9ceeb8d3c8cf1f088be6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/0/340605c5f88cf6864adc5b146c3dffca7a45df22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />. But for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/0/340605c5f88cf6864adc5b146c3dffca7a45df22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />\nwe have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/9/219476dd7b48fa7f91915f9f4f01818bfff15128.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a/x=3/2&lt;\\sqrt[3]5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"130\" height=\"21\" /> and so necessarily <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/a/55afdab16c8c49089c4d9ceeb8d3c8cf1f088be6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/8/c585293a01ee626cd268a8d4ae88f6fae6ea8650.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a/x=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" />.  \nIt follows\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/e/47e5f3980bb5ebb49e6c18f846b3b7dc2be6d459.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac by \\cdot \\frac cz =\\frac 52 \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ (2)\\]\" width=\"130\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><br />\nNote that the definitions of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/5/6f51d57011f1c7cc6b8e9035808e3936ce524817.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"26\" height=\"11\" /> imply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/5/5c53367e194a356986a7d55e325cb14a2496d9c5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y&lt; b/\\sqrt[3]2 &lt; y+1,\\ \\  \\textrm{and} \\ \\ z&lt; c/\\sqrt[3]2 &lt; z+1.\\ \\ \\ \\ (3)\\]\" width=\"386\" height=\"21\" />\nMoreover we have from (2) and from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/1/f41ecebdf18d7d264d6ea987d440cabaceec0229.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b/y\\ge c/z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" /> that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/6/1b6d7ffa3d78d870dba9113572f6851701bd6b50.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac by \\ge \\sqrt{5/2}\\ \\ \\ \\ \\ (4)\\]\" width=\"130\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/6/7d65baaf9671227780dd04ab952911036aa5c868.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/a/d8a3d9994ebd9dbaacc53e5d40500b789641fbfc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b/y=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" /> and we would have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/7/9072fce26c3d16763d4c4babc46b2c71080bdda9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c/z=5/4&lt;\\sqrt[3]2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"21\" />, which contradicts <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/8/b88ea3916e8089c7edbccc3ff91e58e01a6e2682.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>On the other hand, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/d/1cd0c462d531625abfda3b1ab9f60609a7bfdde9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&gt;5$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/e/80e08318d2634855704bbba96ff21e6f7169b15e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y&gt;4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/e/36e7a8675e193d87885a555d2ce063c84fab6f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac by&lt;\\sqrt[3]2(1+\\frac 1y)\\le \\sqrt[3]2(\\frac 54)&lt;\\sqrt{5/2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"267\" height=\"41\" />\nsince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec2762874f806ef481f171330404c6434a3dff2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^2\\cdot \\frac {5^6}{4^6}&lt;\\frac{5^3}{2^3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"93\" height=\"39\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/d/c1dd6764b56bdba318346be09fee4d54b06ca8f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^3&lt;2^7$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"15\" />. So we have only left the \ncases <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/b/61b028a15814a791fe0e139e93c44b8345f0ecda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=3,4,5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" />. But for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/6/626beed3a7eee094ce4b6cf79a49d81669f72d99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=3$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/c/78c7bde5fd6b024cb35216285ee52ddde43cd7d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b/y=3/2&lt;\\sqrt{5/2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"147\" height=\"32\" /> and for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/a/fda5328bc4703ff88e62aa83ea58ae4e8361f5ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> we have \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/7/ed708d57af591bd98b342171dfb961db25910421.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b/y=4/3&lt;\\sqrt{5/2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"147\" height=\"32\" /> and so necessarily <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/6/4f69c1ec597d19324140f3130e9d63367f4b69c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=5$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/6/d864f2af4493ae905a787f344bab47355e0adafc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b/y=5/3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/2/bc261752d13de7e9e681a307b75415b06b2e156b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&gt;\\sqrt{5/2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"64\" height=\"32\" />)\n</p><p>So we arrive finally at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/3/6e3d29da2080fc978ae8418349a7291a18acfe98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=2,b=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/2/47277b3faaa81315d9294cf0fcd5404573cb2a57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c/z=3/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/2/142f715daa1dfa84eb98aac2b5f4e43412db14c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c\\ge 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"40\" height=\"15\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/8/ff8cd45cf90d7d98b27ca4b7fa2219a7d93e1a16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z\\ge 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/7/2a77e3f734379d10982ddda7e99daecc4e0890e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac cz&lt;\\sqrt[3]2(1+\\frac 1z)\\le \\sqrt[3]2(\\frac 76)&lt;\\frac 32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"233\" height=\"37\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/a/a4a194c9f0386278cb589105cd2003302aaae355.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot \\frac {7^3}{6^3}&lt;\\frac{3^3}{2^3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"89\" height=\"41\" />. On the other hand, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/8/038bb6ce6e6a43b79505b8a514d78312fce79927.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c\\le 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" /> there are the only two possible values <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/7/8271d4342b38d2ab38bb626ffad8b9dae00b5e2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=3$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/b/4eb76404ee79952dcc555464b061509299789b09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> which yield the known solutions. \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO\" title=\"1976 IMO\">1976 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1976 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1976 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1976 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1976 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1976 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1976 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1976 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1976 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017172243\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.030 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.043 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 355/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 12234/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.620      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.620      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6414:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017172243 and revision id 143928. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}